WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.980
What should a grafted branch remember?

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.680
In Romans eleven,

3
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.280
Paul pictures Gentile believers as wild olive

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.680
branches grafted into an olive tree.

5
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.460
They now share in its nourishing root.

6
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.460
But Paul gives them a warning:

7
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.260
do not become arrogant toward the other

8
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:20.720
branches.

9
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.380
The branch does not support the root.

10
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.620
The root supports the branch.

11
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.120
The picture points to dependence on God’s

12
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:29.540
covenant blessing.

13
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.400
Gentile believers have received mercy,

14
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.520
and their place gives them no reason

15
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.200
to look down on Jewish people.

16
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.940
Paul says they stand through faith.

17
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.900
When you read this passage,

18
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.000
let that picture check your pride.

19
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.620
Remember the mercy you have received,

20
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.820
and respond with humble gratitude.
